Report an honest POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS from the PM8916 BMS virtual monitor.

The BMS previously reported STATUS=Charging whenever a charger was present
(VBUS online), without checking whether the charger was actually charging.
On this platform the battery-charge-limit monitor holds the battery by
writing 0 to the charger's charge_enabled (clearing CHG_EN while PSTG_EN
keeps the system rail fed from VBUS). In that state the battery is NOT
being charged, yet userspace (and LuCI) kept showing "Charging".

Query the supplying charger's CHARGE_ENABLED property: when it is off the
battery is merely being held, so report POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/pm8916_bms_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pm8916_bms_vm.c
@@ -125,9 +125,25 @@
 
 		if (supplied < 0 && supplied != -ENODEV)
 			return supplied;
-		else if (supplied && supplied != -ENODEV)
-			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
-		else
+		else if (supplied && supplied != -ENODEV) {
+			union power_supply_propval charge = { 0 };
+
+			/*
+			 * The PM8916 LBC charger exposes a writable
+			 * charge_enabled property; when it is off the battery
+			 * is being *held* (the system rail is fed from VBUS via
+			 * PSTG_EN) rather than actually charged.  Report that as
+			 * "Not charging" instead of the misleading "Charging".
+			 * If the supplier does not report the property we fall
+			 * back to "Charging".
+			 */
+			if (power_supply_get_property_from_supplier(psy,
+					POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_ENABLED,
+					&charge) == 0 && !charge.intval)
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
+			else
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+		} else
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 		return 0;
 
